---
const clients = [
  { name: "Claude", detail: "Desktop and claude.ai" },
  { name: "ChatGPT", detail: "Connectors" },
  { name: "Cursor", detail: "And other MCP clients" },
  { name: "Built in", detail: "The in-app assistant" },
];
---

<section class="tight-top" aria-labelledby="mcp-title">
  <div class="wrap mcp">
    <div class="reveal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Works with your AI</span>
      <h2 id="mcp-title">Use it from Claude, ChatGPT or Cursor.</h2>
      <p class="lead">
        Relationship OS is an MCP server. Connect an MCP client and it can read and update your CRM,
        with the same permissions and approval rules as a person. On the free plan, this is how you
        bring your own AI.
      </p>
      <ul class="clients">
        {
          clients.map((client) => (
            <li class="client glass">
              <b>{client.name}</b>
              <span>{client.detail}</span>
            </li>
          ))
        }
      </ul>
      <p class="note">
        Sign in with OAuth and choose read, write or admin access. Revoke it from Settings at any
        time.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="convo glass reveal" aria-label="Example conversation in an AI client">
      <span class="who">In your AI client</span>
      <div class="q">Log a call with Ade at Brightwater. They want the pilot extended to March.</div>
      <span class="tool">activity_create · deal_update</span>
      <div class="r">
        Logged the call on Brightwater Labs. Changing the pilot's close date to 31 March is waiting
        for approval in Relationship OS.
      </div>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>
